job_description:
Diploma and / or Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, IT, Cybersecurity, or relevant qualification; Minimum 5 years of experience in IT security or related field; Solid understanding of basic networking concepts (routing, TCP/IP, DNS, and firewall concepts); Experience with Windows Server administration, including Active Directory (AD), Entra ID, Group Policy, and DNS, will be an advantage; Experience in Identity Security (IAM, PAM, IGA, etc.), including user provisioning, SSO, MFA, privileged account management, access control, and familiarity with protocols such as SAML, OAuth2, OpenID Connect, LDAP, and Kerberos, will be an advantage; Experience with Application Delivery Controller (ADC) solutions, including load balancing (L4/L7), SSL offloading, L7 DDoS protection, and WAF or authentication integration, will be an advantage; Experience in project deployment and implementation is required; Good communication and presentation skills (customer-facing role); Independent, self-motivated, and able to work under pressure; Able to speak English and Bahasa Malaysia;

JOB SUMMARY We are looking for an IT Security Engineer to join our team to design, implement, and support cybersecurity solutions. The ideal candidate should have hands-on experience in system and IT security technologies, be able to perform project deployments, and be confident in conducting technical presentations and solution demonstrations. This role requires someone who can understand customer requirements and deliver practical, secure solutions. ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES Involved in both pre-sales and post-sales engineering activities; Design, implement, and support cybersecurity solutions based on customer requirements; Conduct technical presentations, product demonstrations, and workshops for customers and partners; Work closely with product managers and principals on solution design and proposal; Ensure solutions are designed and implemented based on best practices and security standards; Perform project deployment including installation, configuration, testing, and documentation; Provide troubleshooting and post-deployment support; Collaborate with internal teams to deliver projects within timeline and scope; Keep up-to-date with cybersecurity technologies and trends;

13th month salary Training and career growth Career Development Opportunities Team Building Activities Extra Leave Benefits (only for confirmed employees - marriage leave, compassionate leave) Positive Work Culture Job Rotation or Enrichment Employee Autonomy Annual Leave

Network Security Risk Assessment Security Auditing Firewall Management
